<article class="env-remark" id="0FQ9">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FQ9">Remark <span data-tag="0FQ9">22.13.7</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. Let $A$ be a differential graded $R$-algebra. Let $M^\bullet $ and $N^\bullet $ be complexes of $R$-modules. Let $k \in \mathbf{Z}$ and consider the isomorphism </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits ^\bullet (M^\bullet , N^\bullet )[-k] \longrightarrow \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits ^\bullet (M^\bullet [k], N^\bullet )  \]
</div>
  <p> of complexes of $R$-modules defined in More on Algebra, Item (<a href="/tag/0FNN" data-tag="0FNN">18</a>). If $M^\bullet $ has the structure of a left, resp. right differential graded $A$-module, then this is a map of right, resp. left differential graded $A$-modules (with the module structures as defined in this section). We omit the verification; we warn the reader that the $A$-module structure on the shift of a left graded $A$-module is defined using a sign, see Definition <a href="/tag/0FQ1" data-tag="0FQ1">22.11.3</a>. </p>
</article>